---
id: seo
title: SEO
description: Configure SEO in TanStack Start with page metadata, canonical URLs, structured data, server rendering, sitemaps, and robots.txt.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Looking to optimize for AI assistants and LLMs? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./geo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-is-seo-really","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is SEO, really?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SEO (Search Engine Optimization) is often misunderstood as simply \"showing up on Google\" or a checkbox that a library can magically provide. In reality, SEO is a broad discipline focused on delivering valuable content that people need and making it easy for them to find."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Technical SEO"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a subset of SEO that developers interact with most directly. It involves using tools and APIs that satisfy the technical requirements of search engines, crawlers, rankers, and even LLMs. When someone says a framework has \"good SEO support,\" they typically mean it provides the tools to make this process straightforward."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start provides comprehensive technical SEO capabilities, but you still need to put in the work to use them effectively."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-tanstack-start-provides","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What TanStack Start Provides"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start gives you the building blocks for technical SEO:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-Side Rendering (SSR)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Ensures crawlers receive fully rendered HTML"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Prerendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Pre-generates pages for optimal performance and crawlability"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Document Head Management"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Full control over meta tags, titles, and structured data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Fast load times through code-splitting, streaming, and optimized builds"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"document-head-management","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Document Head Management"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"head"},{"type":"text","value":" property on routes is your primary tool for SEO. It allows you to set page titles, meta descriptions, Open Graph tags, and more."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"basic-meta-tags","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Meta Tags"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: 'My App - Home' },\n      {\n        name: 'description',\n        content: 'Welcome to My App, a platform for...',\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: HomePage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dynamic-meta-tags","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Meta Tags"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use loader data to generate dynamic meta tags for content pages:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"open-graph-and-social-sharing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open Graph and Social Sharing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open Graph tags control how your pages appear when shared on social media:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      // Open Graph\n      { property: 'og:title', content: loaderData.post.title },\n      { property: 'og:description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      { property: 'og:image', content: loaderData.post.coverImage },\n      { property: 'og:type', content: 'article' },\n      // Twitter Card\n      { name: 'twitter:card', content: 'summary_large_image' },\n      { name: 'twitter:title', content: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'twitter:description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      { name: 'twitter:image', content: loaderData.post.coverImage },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"canonical-urls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canonical URLs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canonical URLs help prevent duplicate content issues:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  head: ({ params }) => ({\n    links: [\n      {\n        rel: 'canonical',\n        href: `https://myapp.com/posts/${params.postId}`,\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"structured-data-json-ld","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured Data (JSON-LD)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured data helps search engines understand your content and can enable rich results in search:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.post.title }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Article',\n          headline: loaderData.post.title,\n          description: loaderData.post.excerpt,\n          image: loaderData.post.coverImage,\n          author: {\n            '@type': 'Person',\n            name: loaderData.post.author.name,\n          },\n          datePublished: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-side-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-Side Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR is enabled by default in TanStack Start. This ensures that search engine crawlers receive fully rendered HTML content, which is critical for SEO."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// SSR is automatic - your pages are rendered on the server\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/about')({\n  component: AboutPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For routes that don't need SSR, you can disable it selectively. However, be aware this may impact SEO for those pages:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Only disable SSR for pages that don't need SEO\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  ssr: false, // Dashboard doesn't need to be indexed\n  component: DashboardPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./selective-ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selective SSR guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more details."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"static-prerendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Prerendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For content that doesn't change frequently, static prerendering generates HTML at build time for optimal performance:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title":"rsbuild.config.ts","file":"rsbuild.config.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerendered pages load faster and are easily crawlable. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./static-prerendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Prerendering guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for configuration options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sitemaps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sitemaps"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"built-in-sitemap-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Sitemap Generation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start can automatically generate a sitemap when you enable prerendering with link crawling:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true, // Discovers all linkable pages\n      },\n      sitemap: {\n        enabled: true,\n        host: 'https://myapp.com',\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true, // Discovers all linkable pages\n      },\n      sitemap: {\n        enabled: true,\n        host: 'https://myapp.com',\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title":"rsbuild.config.ts","file":"rsbuild.config.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The sitemap is generated at build time by crawling all discoverable pages from your routes. This is the recommended approach for static or mostly-static sites."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"static-sitemap","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Sitemap"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For simple sites, you can also place a static "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sitemap.xml"},{"type":"text","value":" file in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"public"},{"type":"text","value":" directory:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- public/sitemap.xml -->\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/</loc>\n    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>\n    <priority>1.0</priority>\n  </url>\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/about</loc>\n    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>\n  </url>\n</urlset>","lang":"xml"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This approach works well when your site structure is known and doesn't change often."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dynamic-sitemap","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Sitemap"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For sites with dynamic content that can't be discovered at build time, you can create a dynamic sitemap using a "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server route"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Consider caching this at your CDN for performance:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/sitemap[.]xml.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/sitemap.xml')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const posts = await fetchAllPosts()\n\n        const sitemap = `<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/</loc>\n    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>\n    <priority>1.0</priority>\n  </url>\n  ${posts\n    .map(\n      (post) => `\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/posts/${post.id}</loc>\n    <lastmod>${post.updatedAt}</lastmod>\n    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>\n  </url>`,\n    )\n    .join('')}\n</urlset>`\n\n        return new Response(sitemap, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'application/xml',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"robots-txt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"robots.txt"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"static-robots-txt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static robots.txt"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The simplest approach is to place a static "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"robots.txt"},{"type":"text","value":" file in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"public"},{"type":"text","value":" directory:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// public/robots.txt\nUser-agent: *\nAllow: /\n\nSitemap: https://myapp.com/sitemap.xml","lang":"txt"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This file will be served automatically at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/robots.txt"},{"type":"text","value":". This is the most common approach for most sites."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dynamic-robots-txt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic robots.txt"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more complex scenarios (e.g., different rules per environment), you can create a robots.txt file using a "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server route"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/robots[.]txt.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/robots.txt')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const robots = `User-agent: *\nAllow: /\n\nSitemap: https://myapp.com/sitemap.xml`\n\n        return new Response(robots, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'text/plain',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best Practices"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"performance-matters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance Matters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Page speed is a ranking factor. TanStack Start helps with:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic code-splitting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Only load the JavaScript needed for each page"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming SSR"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Start sending HTML to the browser immediately"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preloading"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Prefetch routes before users navigate to them"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"content-is-king","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Content is King"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Technical SEO is just one piece of the puzzle. The most important factors are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quality content"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Create content that provides value to users"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear site structure"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Organize your routes logically"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Descriptive URLs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Use meaningful path segments ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/my-great-article"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/123"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internal linking"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Help users and crawlers discover your content"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"test-your-implementation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test Your Implementation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use these tools to verify your SEO implementation:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://search.google.com/search-console","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Google Search Console"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Monitor indexing and search performance"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://search.google.com/test/rich-results","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Google Rich Results Test"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Validate structured data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open Graph Debugger"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Preview social sharing cards"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser DevTools - Inspect rendered HTML and meta tags"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"track-your-rankings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Track Your Rankings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To monitor your SEO performance over time, we recommend "},{"type":"link","href":"https://nozzle.io?utm_source=tanstack","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nozzle.io"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Nozzle provides enterprise-grade rank tracking that lets you monitor unlimited keywords, track SERP features, and analyze your visibility against competitors. Unlike traditional rank trackers, Nozzle stores the entire SERP for every query, giving you complete data to understand how your pages perform in search results."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-is-seo-really","text":"What is SEO, really?","level":2},{"id":"what-tanstack-start-provides","text":"What TanStack Start Provides","level":2},{"id":"document-head-management","text":"Document Head Management","level":2},{"id":"basic-meta-tags","text":"Basic Meta Tags","level":3},{"id":"dynamic-meta-tags","text":"Dynamic Meta Tags","level":3},{"id":"open-graph-and-social-sharing","text":"Open Graph and Social Sharing","level":3},{"id":"canonical-urls","text":"Canonical URLs","level":3},{"id":"structured-data-json-ld","text":"Structured Data (JSON-LD)","level":2},{"id":"server-side-rendering","text":"Server-Side Rendering","level":2},{"id":"static-prerendering","text":"Static Prerendering","level":2},{"id":"sitemaps","text":"Sitemaps","level":2},{"id":"built-in-sitemap-generation","text":"Built-in Sitemap Generation","level":3},{"id":"static-sitemap","text":"Static Sitemap","level":3},{"id":"dynamic-sitemap","text":"Dynamic Sitemap","level":3},{"id":"robots-txt","text":"robots.txt","level":2},{"id":"static-robots-txt","text":"Static robots.txt","level":3},{"id":"dynamic-robots-txt","text":"Dynamic robots.txt","level":3},{"id":"best-practices","text":"Best Practices","level":2},{"id":"performance-matters","text":"Performance Matters","level":3},{"id":"content-is-king","text":"Content is King","level":3},{"id":"test-your-implementation","text":"Test Your Implementation","level":3},{"id":"track-your-rankings","text":"Track Your Rankings","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!NOTE]\n> Looking to optimize for AI assistants and LLMs? See the [Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) guide](./geo).\n\n## What is SEO, really?\n\nSEO (Search Engine Optimization) is often misunderstood as simply \"showing up on Google\" or a checkbox that a library can magically provide. In reality, SEO is a broad discipline focused on delivering valuable content that people need and making it easy for them to find.\n\n**Technical SEO** is a subset of SEO that developers interact with most directly. It involves using tools and APIs that satisfy the technical requirements of search engines, crawlers, rankers, and even LLMs. When someone says a framework has \"good SEO support,\" they typically mean it provides the tools to make this process straightforward.\n\nTanStack Start provides comprehensive technical SEO capabilities, but you still need to put in the work to use them effectively.\n\n## What TanStack Start Provides\n\nTanStack Start gives you the building blocks for technical SEO:\n\n- **Server-Side Rendering (SSR)** - Ensures crawlers receive fully rendered HTML\n- **Static Prerendering** - Pre-generates pages for optimal performance and crawlability\n- **Document Head Management** - Full control over meta tags, titles, and structured data\n- **Performance** - Fast load times through code-splitting, streaming, and optimized builds\n\n## Document Head Management\n\nThe `head` property on routes is your primary tool for SEO. It allows you to set page titles, meta descriptions, Open Graph tags, and more.\n\n### Basic Meta Tags\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: 'My App - Home' },\n      {\n        name: 'description',\n        content: 'Welcome to My App, a platform for...',\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: HomePage,\n})\n```\n\n### Dynamic Meta Tags\n\nUse loader data to generate dynamic meta tags for content pages:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Open Graph and Social Sharing\n\nOpen Graph tags control how your pages appear when shared on social media:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      // Open Graph\n      { property: 'og:title', content: loaderData.post.title },\n      { property: 'og:description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      { property: 'og:image', content: loaderData.post.coverImage },\n      { property: 'og:type', content: 'article' },\n      // Twitter Card\n      { name: 'twitter:card', content: 'summary_large_image' },\n      { name: 'twitter:title', content: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'twitter:description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      { name: 'twitter:image', content: loaderData.post.coverImage },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Canonical URLs\n\nCanonical URLs help prevent duplicate content issues:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  head: ({ params }) => ({\n    links: [\n      {\n        rel: 'canonical',\n        href: `https://myapp.com/posts/${params.postId}`,\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n## Structured Data (JSON-LD)\n\nStructured data helps search engines understand your content and can enable rich results in search:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.post.title }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Article',\n          headline: loaderData.post.title,\n          description: loaderData.post.excerpt,\n          image: loaderData.post.coverImage,\n          author: {\n            '@type': 'Person',\n            name: loaderData.post.author.name,\n          },\n          datePublished: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n## Server-Side Rendering\n\nSSR is enabled by default in TanStack Start. This ensures that search engine crawlers receive fully rendered HTML content, which is critical for SEO.\n\n```tsx\n// SSR is automatic - your pages are rendered on the server\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/about')({\n  component: AboutPage,\n})\n```\n\nFor routes that don't need SSR, you can disable it selectively. However, be aware this may impact SEO for those pages:\n\n```tsx\n// Only disable SSR for pages that don't need SEO\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  ssr: false, // Dashboard doesn't need to be indexed\n  component: DashboardPage,\n})\n```\n\nSee the [Selective SSR guide](./selective-ssr) for more details.\n\n## Static Prerendering\n\nFor content that doesn't change frequently, static prerendering generates HTML at build time for optimal performance:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPrerendered pages load faster and are easily crawlable. See the [Static Prerendering guide](./static-prerendering) for configuration options.\n\n## Sitemaps\n\n### Built-in Sitemap Generation\n\nTanStack Start can automatically generate a sitemap when you enable prerendering with link crawling:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true, // Discovers all linkable pages\n      },\n      sitemap: {\n        enabled: true,\n        host: 'https://myapp.com',\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true, // Discovers all linkable pages\n      },\n      sitemap: {\n        enabled: true,\n        host: 'https://myapp.com',\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe sitemap is generated at build time by crawling all discoverable pages from your routes. This is the recommended approach for static or mostly-static sites.\n\n### Static Sitemap\n\nFor simple sites, you can also place a static `sitemap.xml` file in your `public` directory:\n\n```xml\n<!-- public/sitemap.xml -->\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/</loc>\n    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>\n    <priority>1.0</priority>\n  </url>\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/about</loc>\n    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>\n  </url>\n</urlset>\n```\n\nThis approach works well when your site structure is known and doesn't change often.\n\n### Dynamic Sitemap\n\nFor sites with dynamic content that can't be discovered at build time, you can create a dynamic sitemap using a [server route](./server-routes). Consider caching this at your CDN for performance:\n\n```ts\n// src/routes/sitemap[.]xml.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/sitemap.xml')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const posts = await fetchAllPosts()\n\n        const sitemap = `<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/</loc>\n    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>\n    <priority>1.0</priority>\n  </url>\n  ${posts\n    .map(\n      (post) => `\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/posts/${post.id}</loc>\n    <lastmod>${post.updatedAt}</lastmod>\n    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>\n  </url>`,\n    )\n    .join('')}\n</urlset>`\n\n        return new Response(sitemap, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'application/xml',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## robots.txt\n\n### Static robots.txt\n\nThe simplest approach is to place a static `robots.txt` file in your `public` directory:\n\n```txt\n// public/robots.txt\nUser-agent: *\nAllow: /\n\nSitemap: https://myapp.com/sitemap.xml\n```\n\nThis file will be served automatically at `/robots.txt`. This is the most common approach for most sites.\n\n### Dynamic robots.txt\n\nFor more complex scenarios (e.g., different rules per environment), you can create a robots.txt file using a [server route](./server-routes):\n\n```ts\n// src/routes/robots[.]txt.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/robots.txt')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const robots = `User-agent: *\nAllow: /\n\nSitemap: https://myapp.com/sitemap.xml`\n\n        return new Response(robots, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'text/plain',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Performance Matters\n\nPage speed is a ranking factor. TanStack Start helps with:\n\n- **Automatic code-splitting** - Only load the JavaScript needed for each page\n- **Streaming SSR** - Start sending HTML to the browser immediately\n- **Preloading** - Prefetch routes before users navigate to them\n\n### Content is King\n\nTechnical SEO is just one piece of the puzzle. The most important factors are:\n\n- **Quality content** - Create content that provides value to users\n- **Clear site structure** - Organize your routes logically\n- **Descriptive URLs** - Use meaningful path segments (`/posts/my-great-article` vs `/posts/123`)\n- **Internal linking** - Help users and crawlers discover your content\n\n### Test Your Implementation\n\nUse these tools to verify your SEO implementation:\n\n- [Google Search Console](https://search.google.com/search-console) - Monitor indexing and search performance\n- [Google Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results) - Validate structured data\n- [Open Graph Debugger](https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/) - Preview social sharing cards\n- Browser DevTools - Inspect rendered HTML and meta tags\n\n### Track Your Rankings\n\nTo monitor your SEO performance over time, we recommend [Nozzle.io](https://nozzle.io?utm_source=tanstack). Nozzle provides enterprise-grade rank tracking that lets you monitor unlimited keywords, track SERP features, and analyze your visibility against competitors. Unlike traditional rank trackers, Nozzle stores the entire SERP for every query, giving you complete data to understand how your pages perform in search results.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: seo\ntitle: SEO\ndescription: Configure SEO in TanStack Start with page metadata, canonical URLs, structured data, server rendering, sitemaps, and robots.txt.\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Looking to optimize for AI assistants and LLMs? See the [Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) guide](./geo).\n\n## What is SEO, really?\n\nSEO (Search Engine Optimization) is often misunderstood as simply \"showing up on Google\" or a checkbox that a library can magically provide. In reality, SEO is a broad discipline focused on delivering valuable content that people need and making it easy for them to find.\n\n**Technical SEO** is a subset of SEO that developers interact with most directly. It involves using tools and APIs that satisfy the technical requirements of search engines, crawlers, rankers, and even LLMs. When someone says a framework has \"good SEO support,\" they typically mean it provides the tools to make this process straightforward.\n\nTanStack Start provides comprehensive technical SEO capabilities, but you still need to put in the work to use them effectively.\n\n## What TanStack Start Provides\n\nTanStack Start gives you the building blocks for technical SEO:\n\n- **Server-Side Rendering (SSR)** - Ensures crawlers receive fully rendered HTML\n- **Static Prerendering** - Pre-generates pages for optimal performance and crawlability\n- **Document Head Management** - Full control over meta tags, titles, and structured data\n- **Performance** - Fast load times through code-splitting, streaming, and optimized builds\n\n## Document Head Management\n\nThe `head` property on routes is your primary tool for SEO. It allows you to set page titles, meta descriptions, Open Graph tags, and more.\n\n### Basic Meta Tags\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: 'My App - Home' },\n      {\n        name: 'description',\n        content: 'Welcome to My App, a platform for...',\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: HomePage,\n})\n```\n\n### Dynamic Meta Tags\n\nUse loader data to generate dynamic meta tags for content pages:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Open Graph and Social Sharing\n\nOpen Graph tags control how your pages appear when shared on social media:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      // Open Graph\n      { property: 'og:title', content: loaderData.post.title },\n      { property: 'og:description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      { property: 'og:image', content: loaderData.post.coverImage },\n      { property: 'og:type', content: 'article' },\n      // Twitter Card\n      { name: 'twitter:card', content: 'summary_large_image' },\n      { name: 'twitter:title', content: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'twitter:description', content: loaderData.post.excerpt },\n      { name: 'twitter:image', content: loaderData.post.coverImage },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Canonical URLs\n\nCanonical URLs help prevent duplicate content issues:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  head: ({ params }) => ({\n    links: [\n      {\n        rel: 'canonical',\n        href: `https://myapp.com/posts/${params.postId}`,\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n## Structured Data (JSON-LD)\n\nStructured data helps search engines understand your content and can enable rich results in search:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.post.title }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Article',\n          headline: loaderData.post.title,\n          description: loaderData.post.excerpt,\n          image: loaderData.post.coverImage,\n          author: {\n            '@type': 'Person',\n            name: loaderData.post.author.name,\n          },\n          datePublished: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n## Server-Side Rendering\n\nSSR is enabled by default in TanStack Start. This ensures that search engine crawlers receive fully rendered HTML content, which is critical for SEO.\n\n```tsx\n// SSR is automatic - your pages are rendered on the server\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/about')({\n  component: AboutPage,\n})\n```\n\nFor routes that don't need SSR, you can disable it selectively. However, be aware this may impact SEO for those pages:\n\n```tsx\n// Only disable SSR for pages that don't need SEO\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  ssr: false, // Dashboard doesn't need to be indexed\n  component: DashboardPage,\n})\n```\n\nSee the [Selective SSR guide](./selective-ssr) for more details.\n\n## Static Prerendering\n\nFor content that doesn't change frequently, static prerendering generates HTML at build time for optimal performance:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPrerendered pages load faster and are easily crawlable. See the [Static Prerendering guide](./static-prerendering) for configuration options.\n\n## Sitemaps\n\n### Built-in Sitemap Generation\n\nTanStack Start can automatically generate a sitemap when you enable prerendering with link crawling:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true, // Discovers all linkable pages\n      },\n      sitemap: {\n        enabled: true,\n        host: 'https://myapp.com',\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        enabled: true,\n        crawlLinks: true, // Discovers all linkable pages\n      },\n      sitemap: {\n        enabled: true,\n        host: 'https://myapp.com',\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe sitemap is generated at build time by crawling all discoverable pages from your routes. This is the recommended approach for static or mostly-static sites.\n\n### Static Sitemap\n\nFor simple sites, you can also place a static `sitemap.xml` file in your `public` directory:\n\n```xml\n<!-- public/sitemap.xml -->\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/</loc>\n    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>\n    <priority>1.0</priority>\n  </url>\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/about</loc>\n    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>\n  </url>\n</urlset>\n```\n\nThis approach works well when your site structure is known and doesn't change often.\n\n### Dynamic Sitemap\n\nFor sites with dynamic content that can't be discovered at build time, you can create a dynamic sitemap using a [server route](./server-routes). Consider caching this at your CDN for performance:\n\n```ts\n// src/routes/sitemap[.]xml.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/sitemap.xml')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const posts = await fetchAllPosts()\n\n        const sitemap = `<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\">\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/</loc>\n    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>\n    <priority>1.0</priority>\n  </url>\n  ${posts\n    .map(\n      (post) => `\n  <url>\n    <loc>https://myapp.com/posts/${post.id}</loc>\n    <lastmod>${post.updatedAt}</lastmod>\n    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>\n  </url>`,\n    )\n    .join('')}\n</urlset>`\n\n        return new Response(sitemap, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'application/xml',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## robots.txt\n\n### Static robots.txt\n\nThe simplest approach is to place a static `robots.txt` file in your `public` directory:\n\n```txt\n// public/robots.txt\nUser-agent: *\nAllow: /\n\nSitemap: https://myapp.com/sitemap.xml\n```\n\nThis file will be served automatically at `/robots.txt`. This is the most common approach for most sites.\n\n### Dynamic robots.txt\n\nFor more complex scenarios (e.g., different rules per environment), you can create a robots.txt file using a [server route](./server-routes):\n\n```ts\n// src/routes/robots[.]txt.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/robots.txt')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const robots = `User-agent: *\nAllow: /\n\nSitemap: https://myapp.com/sitemap.xml`\n\n        return new Response(robots, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'text/plain',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Performance Matters\n\nPage speed is a ranking factor. TanStack Start helps with:\n\n- **Automatic code-splitting** - Only load the JavaScript needed for each page\n- **Streaming SSR** - Start sending HTML to the browser immediately\n- **Preloading** - Prefetch routes before users navigate to them\n\n### Content is King\n\nTechnical SEO is just one piece of the puzzle. The most important factors are:\n\n- **Quality content** - Create content that provides value to users\n- **Clear site structure** - Organize your routes logically\n- **Descriptive URLs** - Use meaningful path segments (`/posts/my-great-article` vs `/posts/123`)\n- **Internal linking** - Help users and crawlers discover your content\n\n### Test Your Implementation\n\nUse these tools to verify your SEO implementation:\n\n- [Google Search Console](https://search.google.com/search-console) - Monitor indexing and search performance\n- [Google Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results) - Validate structured data\n- [Open Graph Debugger](https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/) - Preview social sharing cards\n- Browser DevTools - Inspect rendered HTML and meta tags\n\n### Track Your Rankings\n\nTo monitor your SEO performance over time, we recommend [Nozzle.io](https://nozzle.io?utm_source=tanstack). Nozzle provides enterprise-grade rank tracking that lets you monitor unlimited keywords, track SERP features, and analyze your visibility against competitors. Unlike traditional rank trackers, Nozzle stores the entire SERP for every query, giving you complete data to understand how your pages perform in search results.\n"}
